(6373038, 944568, 83313, '<td valign="top">I love these old rusty-crusties, but you saved your image with a ton of compression, which is killing a good shot. There are compression artifacts all over the place in this photo. It''s most prominent on the door, but the compression is taking away valuable detail throughout the image. With a file size of only 30k, you had a ton of overhead to fit a lot more detail in this. Compression kills detail. Always use the least amount of compression you can get away with and still come in under the challenge limit<br/> <br/>The lesser issue is the image size. You could have used up to 800 pixels on the long edge, which would have again fit much more detail into the scene. If you choose to do a re-edit, I would love to see the results.</td>', 'I love these old rusty-crusties, but you saved your image with a ton of compression, which is killing a good shot. There are compression artifacts all over the place in this photo. It''s most prominent on the door, but the compression is taking away valuable detail throughout the image. With a file size of only 30k, you had a ton of overhead to fit a lot more detail in this. Compression kills detail. Always use the least amount of compression you can get away with and still come in under the challenge limit The lesser issue is the image size. You could have used up to 800 pixels on the long edge, which would have again fit much more detail into the scene. If you choose to do a re-edit, I would love to see the results.', '2011-04-04 17:44:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373050, 944591, 40391, '<td valign="top">Great tones - great stare.  This looks like a Spiffy image.  Well done.</td>', 'Great tones - great stare.  This looks like a Spiffy image.  Well done.', '2011-04-04 18:04:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373053, 944011, 96751, '<td valign="top">Ah, those were the days.</td>', 'Ah, those were the days.', '2011-04-04 18:06:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373061, 944553, 96751, '<td valign="top">Great b/w bokeh!</td>', 'Great b/w bokeh!', '2011-04-04 18:12:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373062, 944579, 96751, '<td valign="top">Nice cool spot for a summer picnic!  Beautiful and moody</td>', 'Nice cool spot for a summer picnic!  Beautiful and moody', '2011-04-04 18:12:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373083, 944206, 16106, '<td valign="top">A bit strong with the filters; the fabric looks almost plastic, or like very new shiny satin, which is at odds with the frayed ends. Nice framing, sense of flow and very nice tones</td>', 'A bit strong with the filters; the fabric looks almost plastic, or like very new shiny satin, which is at odds with the frayed ends. Nice framing, sense of flow and very nice tones', '2011-04-04 18:28:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373092, 944398, 16106, '<td valign="top">The lighting and framing are quite good, but that is a very awkward pose. her face says quite reflection and her hand seems to be in the middle of a rude gesture or a phrase of ASL.</td>', 'The lighting and framing are quite good, but that is a very awkward pose. her face says quite reflection and her hand seems to be in the middle of a rude gesture or a phrase of ASL.', '2011-04-04 18:39:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373096, 944367, 16106, '<td valign="top">Nice capture of a moment, its a shame the cyclone fence is in focus and the front dog is not. My eye keeps being drawn off by that expanse on highly detailed fence that adds nothing to the composition.</td>', 'Nice capture of a moment, its a shame the cyclone fence is in focus and the front dog is not. My eye keeps being drawn off by that expanse on highly detailed fence that adds nothing to the composition.', '2011-04-04 18:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373099, 944421, 16106, '<td valign="top">The lighting and texture on the ball are great, but the glove ( im guessing the ball is in a  feilder''s glove) cuts off the circle of the ball and is so vague and has so little information that it''s major effect is as a negative. So partial wow! and partial huh?</td>', 'The lighting and texture on the ball are great, but the glove ( im guessing the ball is in a  feilder''s glove) cuts off the circle of the ball and is so vague and has so little information that it''s major effect is as a negative. So partial wow! and partial huh?', '2011-04-04 18:48:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373100, 944264, 108069, '<td valign="top">Very nice movement. I''m not voting, but I''ll critique this anyway because I like photos like this where I actually might have a decent suggestion. Emphasis on <i>might</i>. <br/> <br/>As powerful and impressive as the motion of the wave is, I''ll contradict myself now and say the photo to me is too busy. And I think that is because it''s a tight crop and the border does not suit the crop. I might have pulled back off this crop a little to get a greater sense of perspective of the scene, or had the water rushing in from out of frame more (compositional preferences only), but my main issue is that I feel the thick, white lines overpower the white of the wave, and also contradict the lines in the wave, which are running near vertical. I think if you were to ditch those white lines (or at a minimum reduce them to a pixel wide each and soften the white (maybe pulling the white from the wave with the eyedrop tool)) this would be a much stronger and less confusing image.<br/> <br/>I typically don''t give a damn about borders, but this seems like a really quick way to improve this photo.<br/> <br/>Keep in mind I''m not a good photographer, but as a viewer, that''s what I see.</td>', 'Very nice movement. I''m not voting, but I''ll critique this anyway because I like photos like this where I actually might have a decent suggestion. Emphasis on might.  As powerful and impressive as the motion of the wave is, I''ll contradict myself now and say the photo to me is too busy. And I think that is because it''s a tight crop and the border does not suit the crop. I might have pulled back off this crop a little to get a greater sense of perspective of the scene, or had the water rushing in from out of frame more (compositional preferences only), but my main issue is that I feel the thick, white lines overpower the white of the wave, and also contradict the lines in the wave, which are running near vertical. I think if you were to ditch those white lines (or at a minimum reduce them to a pixel wide each and soften the white (maybe pulling the white from the wave with the eyedrop tool)) this would be a much stronger and less confusing image. I typically don''t give a damn about borders, but this seems like a really quick way to improve this photo. Keep in mind I''m not a good photographer, but as a viewer, that''s what I see.', '2011-04-04 18:50:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373104, 944379, 108069, '<td valign="top">This looks like some fancy SEP work here, or at least something I''m unable to replicate. Excellent tones and light values throughout. Makes the image. Nice.</td>', 'This looks like some fancy SEP work here, or at least something I''m unable to replicate. Excellent tones and light values throughout. Makes the image. Nice.', '2011-04-04 18:52:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6373113, 943919, 108069, '<td valign="top">Wonderful tonal range and contrast throughout the entire image. Exposed perfectly to get the texture in the foreground. There''s a bit of an optical illusion at about 5:30 that initially looked like a drop on the lens. It''s obviously a motion-blurred bit, but it would bug me if I had this hanging on my wall. And it''s at that caliber. Fantastic photo.</td>', 'Wonderful tonal range and contrast throughout the entire image. Exposed perfectly to get the texture in the foreground. There''s a bit of an optical illusion at about 5:30 that initially looked like a drop on the lens. It''s obviously a motion-blurred bit, but it would bug me if I had this hanging on my wall. And it''s at that caliber. Fantastic photo.', '2011-04-04 18:57:52.000000', NULL, 1),
