(6377165, 943888, 76335, '<td valign="top">This almost feels macabre -- the piercing stare and coldness of it all. That''s not to say I don''t like it.</td>', 'This almost feels macabre -- the piercing stare and coldness of it all. That''s not to say I don''t like it.', '2011-04-06 20:47:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377166, 944364, 76335, '<td valign="top">I''ll bet he plays like Charlie Parker too.</td>', 'I''ll bet he plays like Charlie Parker too.', '2011-04-06 20:49:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377388, 944471, 75001, '<td valign="top">Good sharp capture but I feel you have cropped this very tight. More spaces round the bird would have made this better</td>', 'Good sharp capture but I feel you have cropped this very tight. More spaces round the bird would have made this better', '2011-04-07 02:07:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377461, 944181, 117474, '<td valign="top">Nice subject and textures. I like that branch--what an odd direction it''s going in! I like the lines that the branches make. Especially the ''why''-ing branch. How bizarre nature is sometimes, eh? Interesting subject, and well captured. It''s nicely in focus. Sharp. And black and white suits this quite well and encourages texturing--definitely suits the criteria of the challenge. No question in my book. <br/> <br/>Critiques (these are my personal feelings about how I might have done things different... it doesn''t mean they should be done or that they''d make it better--I''m far from being an experienced photographer myself--I just know what I like, and my critiques will tend to suggest editing towards that direction):<br/>Somehow this image doesn''t seem to... pop for me. Not saying it doesn''t, but I don''t feel as much depth in this as I think I could/should with the branch that''s going backwards so far. That might have potential to seem really deep. If I was to try to get this I might run the image through topaz adjust. That does a really good job at it, in my opinion. <br/>This is more of a personal thing, but I dig high contrasted images so I personally would have liked to have seen more contrast. Maybe just over the trunk though, because if done on the leaves it might make them too dark.<br/>The crop doesn''t do much for the image for me... were you to crop just to the left of where the ''why'' branch branches off from the main left trunk (somewhere between a third and quarter from the left) it would have given a spiral effect on the tree which would have probably encouraged higher scoring. <br/> <br/>It''s a fine image. The leaves do you credit because if they weren''t there I''d imaging the tree would be quite twiggy which would make the image far more difficult to look at and discern details. <br/>I can''t decide between 6 or 7 for this one. I''d say probably 6. But certainly 6.5 if it was there :-)</td>', 'Nice subject and textures. I like that branch--what an odd direction it''s going in! I like the lines that the branches make. Especially the ''why''-ing branch. How bizarre nature is sometimes, eh? Interesting subject, and well captured. It''s nicely in focus. Sharp. And black and white suits this quite well and encourages texturing--definitely suits the criteria of the challenge. No question in my book.  Critiques (these are my personal feelings about how I might have done things different... it doesn''t mean they should be done or that they''d make it better--I''m far from being an experienced photographer myself--I just know what I like, and my critiques will tend to suggest editing towards that direction):Somehow this image doesn''t seem to... pop for me. Not saying it doesn''t, but I don''t feel as much depth in this as I think I could/should with the branch that''s going backwards so far. That might have potential to seem really deep. If I was to try to get this I might run the image through topaz adjust. That does a really good job at it, in my opinion. This is more of a personal thing, but I dig high contrasted images so I personally would have liked to have seen more contrast. Maybe just over the trunk though, because if done on the leaves it might make them too dark.The crop doesn''t do much for the image for me... were you to crop just to the left of where the ''why'' branch branches off from the main left trunk (somewhere between a third and quarter from the left) it would have given a spiral effect on the tree which would have probably encouraged higher scoring.  It''s a fine image. The leaves do you credit because if they weren''t there I''d imaging the tree would be quite twiggy which would make the image far more difficult to look at and discern details. I can''t decide between 6 or 7 for this one. I''d say probably 6. But certainly 6.5 if it was there :-)', '2011-04-07 05:28:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377506, 944578, 108069, '<td valign="top">There''s great movement that pulls you into the significant depth of this photo. Like there''s a giant sucker in the sky somewhere out there. That was not a crack on religion. Great texture in the grass and detail in the clouds. Really, really nice.</td>', 'There''s great movement that pulls you into the significant depth of this photo. Like there''s a giant sucker in the sky somewhere out there. That was not a crack on religion. Great texture in the grass and detail in the clouds. Really, really nice.', '2011-04-07 07:23:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377575, 943419, 57447, '<td valign="top">I like your compisition and the movement you have conveyed.</td>', 'I like your compisition and the movement you have conveyed.', '2011-04-07 10:28:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377587, 944405, 108069, '<td valign="top">The contrast is quite nice and the composition is interesting with the lines on the slope. If you could have gotten a bit more gradient in the sky, fading from grey to white, and just more tonal range overall (this seems dark and light only) this would be a truly excellent photo. Not voting, just commenting.</td>', 'The contrast is quite nice and the composition is interesting with the lines on the slope. If you could have gotten a bit more gradient in the sky, fading from grey to white, and just more tonal range overall (this seems dark and light only) this would be a truly excellent photo. Not voting, just commenting.', '2011-04-07 10:52:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377590, 943733, 108069, '<td valign="top">Nice texture. Like two overlapping documents, one or both of which are frayed. Nice lines. I prefer a wider range or transition of grey tones to the black vs. white, but I like this image a lot.</td>', 'Nice texture. Like two overlapping documents, one or both of which are frayed. Nice lines. I prefer a wider range or transition of grey tones to the black vs. white, but I like this image a lot.', '2011-04-07 10:55:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377591, 944540, 108069, '<td valign="top">Well composed. Nice use of those blinds and natural light to set off an interesting B&amp;W image. Smooth and subtle.</td>', 'Well composed. Nice use of those blinds and natural light to set off an interesting B&W image. Smooth and subtle.', '2011-04-07 10:57:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377595, 943902, 108069, '<td valign="top">There is a really interesting phenomenon occurring with the composition here. As expected, my eye starts with the lines on that post near the corner, follows along to the left, the other fence to the barn, take a good look at the barn, along the back fence to the right, and then back to the corner, to do it all over again. And again. My eyes are penned in by the pen! It''s really interesting, and if it was on purpose it''s masterful. Hell, even by mistake it''s quite a cool viewing experience.<br/> <br/>I think the rather bland sky and the detail-less hills in the distance lend to this experience. There really isn''t anything higher int he shot to distract.<br/> <br/>I do also like how the barn is a bit silvery, which does set it off a bit from the rest of the shot. Great photo.</td>', 'There is a really interesting phenomenon occurring with the composition here. As expected, my eye starts with the lines on that post near the corner, follows along to the left, the other fence to the barn, take a good look at the barn, along the back fence to the right, and then back to the corner, to do it all over again. And again. My eyes are penned in by the pen! It''s really interesting, and if it was on purpose it''s masterful. Hell, even by mistake it''s quite a cool viewing experience. I think the rather bland sky and the detail-less hills in the distance lend to this experience. There really isn''t anything higher int he shot to distract. I do also like how the barn is a bit silvery, which does set it off a bit from the rest of the shot. Great photo.', '2011-04-07 11:05:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377597, 943256, 108069, '<td valign="top">Lovely detail and nice focal depth to avoid the annoying out of focus flower (the one guy doesn''t count). Nice compositions as well. Nicely done.</td>', 'Lovely detail and nice focal depth to avoid the annoying out of focus flower (the one guy doesn''t count). Nice compositions as well. Nicely done.', '2011-04-07 11:06:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377601, 944591, 108069, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice portrait. Great detail, sharp where it needs to be. And the composition is quite interesting in that his right eye seems hopeful while his left eye seems a bit sad, as though the juxtaposition with the black is negative and the brighter background has a bit of promise. Great image.</td>', 'Very, very nice portrait. Great detail, sharp where it needs to be. And the composition is quite interesting in that his right eye seems hopeful while his left eye seems a bit sad, as though the juxtaposition with the black is negative and the brighter background has a bit of promise. Great image.', '2011-04-07 11:09:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377606, 944224, 108069, '<td valign="top">Great title. It''s as if we are on the outside, peering through a natural frame into a different world. Nice depth. I''m leaning in to see what I can see. Is that a twister?! Well done.</td>', 'Great title. It''s as if we are on the outside, peering through a natural frame into a different world. Nice depth. I''m leaning in to see what I can see. Is that a twister?! Well done.', '2011-04-07 11:11:08.000000', NULL, 1),
